  "articleBody": "Embarking on home exterior improvements is exciting, but it’s easy to stumble if you’re not careful. Avoiding common pitfalls can save you time, money, and a lot of headaches down the road. One of the biggest mistakes is jumping into a project without confirming local permit requirements. Depending on what you’re doing, you might need one, and starting without it could lead to fines or rework. Another frequent misstep is accepting verbal promises instead of getting everything in writing. Always insist on a detailed, written contract that outlines the full scope of work, materials, timeline, and costs. Be wary of unusually low bids; sometimes, these come with hidden exclusions or lower-quality materials that cost more in the long run. It's much better to compare bids based on the exact same scope of work. \n\n**Common Mistakes to Avoid**\n- **Starting without permits:** Many exterior projects require local permits. Always check with your municipality first; your contractor should also be familiar with these requirements.\n- **Relying on verbal agreements:** Get every detail of the work, materials, timeline, and cost in a written contract. This protects both you and the contractor.\n- **Choosing the lowest bid blindly:** An unusually low bid might mean corners are being cut or essential items are excluded. Ensure you’re comparing apples to apples across quotes.\n- **Not verifying insurance:** Always confirm that your contractor’s insurance is active. You can contact their insurer directly to be sure; this protects you from liability.\n- **Neglecting manufacturer warranties and final receipts:** Keep all documentation for materials and services. This is crucial for future warranty claims or property records.\n\nDiscounted Roofing Co. emphasizes guiding customers step-by-step through projects, including the often-confusing parts like insurance claims and project documentation. They focus on honest communication and quality craftsmanship. Doing your homework and getting all details squared away helps ensure your project goes smoothly and gives you peace of mind. \n\nHave questions about your upcoming exterior project? Reach out to Discounted Roofing Co. for expert guidance and a free estimate.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-03"
}